Let's denote $X=(x \mathbf{I} + y \mathbf{A})^2$. Expanding, we get
\[X=(x^2 i^2)(\mathbf{I}^2)+xy\mathbf{I}\mathbf{A}+1(xy\mathbf{A}\mathbf{I})+y^2\mathbf{A}^2.\]
\[\left \{ 
\begin{align*}(x^2i^2)\mathbf{I}^2&= \mathbf{I} \\[1.2ex] xy\mathbf{I}\mathbf{A} + 1(xy\mathbf{A}\mathbf{I}) &= \mathbf{A} \\[1.2ex] y^2\mathbf{A}^2 &=\mathbf{A}
\end{align*}
\right. \]
Therefore, $x=1$ and $y=1.$</think> <answer> $(1, 1)$ </answer>

